From ecee9e071354e59cf1d9fff2af1668a8d2e63110 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:45:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pcid: BCM2711 PCIe host bridge; rpi-firmwared: VL805 firmware
 load (#305)

pcid brings up the Raspberry Pi 4 family's PCIe bridge (brcm,bcm2711-pcie):
reset, SerDes, inbound window from dma-ranges, outbound window from ranges,
link; config access through the root port's registers and the index/data
window; one bus behind the root port with the device's memory BARs in the
outbound window. BARs go to drivers as CPU addresses. For the VL805 it asks
rpi-firmwared, through the new write-only file xhci_reset
(NOTIFY_XHCI_RESET), to load the USB controller's firmware. Then pcid-spawner
starts xhcid as on other machines.

The register arithmetic and devicetree cell parsing are in
brcmstb_layout.rs, with host tests (rustc --edition 2021 --test).
